From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:15:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/haswell: Put the backlight level back at wake under
 macOS

On resume from S3, gma_setup_panel() starts the backlight PWM at a 50%
duty cycle. Linux and Windows set their own level again; macOS keeps
the 50% until a brightness key is pressed, when XBQC finds the PWM away
from BRLV and applies BRLV again.

In _WAK, under macOS (ISDW) and once BRLV holds a level (BRVA, set when
_BCM sets one or _BQC reads one), call XBCM with BRLV, as the next key
press would. The other OSes run the same _WAK as before.

TEST=Built lenovo/w541 with mrc.bin and with the native RAM init. In
acpiexec, with BCLM 100, the PWM (BCLV) at 50 and BRLV 77 with BRVA set:
with _OSI ("Darwin") installed, _WAK (3) sets BCLV to 77, while _WAK
(4), or _WAK (3) with BRVA clear, leaves it at 50; without _OSI
("Darwin"), _WAK leaves it at 50 in all three cases.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/platform.asl | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/platform.asl b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/platform.asl
index 07381b80e3..4297baf47e 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/platform.asl
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/platform.asl
@@ -5,6 +5,15 @@ Method(_WAK,1)
 	/* Wake the HKEY to init BT/WWAN */
 	\_SB.PCI0.LPCB.EC.HKEY.WAKE (Arg0)
 
+	/*
+	 * The resume path sets the backlight PWM to 50% (gma_setup_panel()).
+	 * Linux and Windows set their own level again, macOS keeps that one:
+	 * there, put back the last level that _BCM set or _BQC read (BRLV).
+	 */
+	If (Arg0 == 3 && \ISDW () && \_SB.PCI0.GFX0.BRVA) {
+		\_SB.PCI0.GFX0.XBCM (\_SB.PCI0.GFX0.BRLV)
+	}
+
 	Return(Package(){0,0})
 }
 
